\use{book}

\title{A Short Book}
\author{Typeset with the \texttt{book} package}
\date{texish}

\frontmatter
\maketitle

\chapter{Preface}

This book is set with the \texttt{book} package, the \texttt{book}-class companion to
the \texttt{document} package's article format. Front matter like this preface carries
lowercase-roman folios and unnumbered chapters, just as in LaTeX.

The page number at the foot of this page is a roman numeral, and the chapter title
above carries no number. When the main matter begins, the folios restart at arabic~1
and chapters take numbers, with sections numbered within their chapter.

\mainmatter

\part{Foundations}

\chapter{Introduction}

The main matter numbers its chapters and restarts the folio at one. This is
Chapter~1, and the page at the foot now reads an arabic numeral. Sections beneath a
chapter carry the chapter as a prefix, so the first section below is numbered 1.1.

\section{Background}

A section's number is the chapter number and the section number joined with a dot. A
new chapter resets the section counter, so the first section of every chapter is
always \emph{n}.1. The running head at the top of the page shows the chapter title,
recorded as a page mark when the chapter opened.

\subsection{A finer point}

Subsections add a third level, numbered within the section: this one is 1.1.1. The
document package's lists, quotations and emphasis are all inherited unchanged, so a
book can use them without redeclaring anything.

\begin{quote}
A quotation block is indented on both sides and reverts to the body margins when it
ends, because the environment sets its margins inside its own group.
\end{quote}

\section{A second section}

This second section of the introduction numbers as 1.2. Because figures and tables are
also numbered within the chapter, the figure below is Figure~1.1 — the first figure of
Chapter~1 — and a figure in the next chapter would restart at 2.1.

\begin{itemize}
\item Chapters open a fresh page and set a running head.
\item Sections, subsections, figures and tables number within the chapter.
\item Front matter is roman and unnumbered; the main matter restarts at arabic one.
\end{itemize}

\chapter{A second chapter}

This is Chapter~2. Its sections restart at 2.1, and the running head at the top of the
page now names this chapter rather than the introduction. The folio at the foot keeps
counting in arabic numerals from where the previous chapter left off.

\section{Carrying on}

Nothing here is new; this section exists only to push the document onto a further page
so the running head and folio can be seen to follow the chapter across a page break.
The body text wraps and justifies exactly as the document package sets it, since the
book package changes only the sectioning, the title page, and the page numbering.

\backmatter

\chapter{Afterword}

Back matter unnumbers chapters again but keeps the arabic folio running, so an
afterword, bibliography or index reads as a titled chapter without a number while the
page count continues unbroken from the main matter.
